      <p>
        I&rsquo;m Link &mdash; a backend and systems engineer. I work on real-time
        messaging systems, network internals, and high-performance services, mostly
        in Go and C++.
      </p>
      <p>
        This blog is where I write up the problems I find interesting: protocol and
        kernel-level debugging, the architecture of systems that hold millions of
        live connections, and the trade-offs behind them. Posts aim for the level of
        detail I&rsquo;d want to read myself &mdash; mechanisms over hand-waving.
      </p>
